{
  "_id": "fhSubBlackLift01",
  "name": "Black Lift",
  "type": "consumable",
  "img": "icons/svg/item-bag.svg",
  "folder": "fhSubModern00001",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>An oil-based stack of underground origin. Used responsibly it produces a measurable strength gain; used carelessly it produces a coroner's report. Discipline is the difference, and discipline is written down.</p><p><strong><em>Desired effects on use.</em></strong> For 10 minutes you gain a +2 bonus to Strength (Athletics) checks, a +1 bonus to Strength-based weapon attack rolls, and your walking speed increases by 5 feet.</p><p><strong><em>On use, save against addiction.</em></strong> Make a DC 15 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, you gain the Addicted condition from Black Lift (see below).</p><p><strong><em>Addicted from Black Lift.</em></strong> While you have this Addicted condition, you are also Poisoned, have disadvantage on Constitution saving throws, and your walking speed is reduced by 5 feet.</p><p><strong><em>Withdrawal.</em></strong> At the end of each Long Rest while addicted, you either take another dose or abstain. If you abstain, make a DC 14 Wisdom check to resist the craving; on a failure, you give in and take a dose. On a success, make a DC 30 Constitution saving throw; on a failed save, you suffer withdrawal for 3 days. If you have no doses left, skip the Wisdom check and make the saving throw. While in withdrawal, abstaining takes only the Wisdom check, and taking any dose ends the withdrawal but not the addiction. When the withdrawal ends, so does the addiction.</p><p><em>Requires ready paraphernalia that applies to ingested substances, such as a Tincture Dropper or an Athlete's Logbook.</em></p>"
    },
